## Why comparisons are not units of heat

Redundant comparisons can lengthen every path without changing the sorting map. Move the slider to separate tree depth from information erased.

{{interactive_demo:2}}

{{visualization:2}}

<details><summary>Click to reveal the padding proof</summary>

Place a branch above a tree and send both outcomes to identical copies. One level is added to every path and the leaves are duplicated. Repeating this $r$ times raises height from $h$ to $h+r$. The computed map still collapses the same $n!$ permutations to one output, so it still erases $\log_2(n!)$ bits when no history is retained.

</details>

