## Scaling and physical interpretation

The plot compares exact factorial information with its leading $n\log_2 n$ scale.

{{visualization:0}}

Landauer's principle prices information that is actually reset, not questions that happen to be asked. For background, see [Landauer's principle](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Landauer%27s_principle), [reversible computing](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reversible_computing), and [comparison sorting](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comparison_sort).

<details><summary>Click to reveal assumptions and limitations</summary>

The finite-set entropy uses a uniform prior over permutations. The tree condition counts transcript capacity but does not encode comparison semantics. The work $kT\log(n!)$ is an ideal quasistatic baseline for discarding the input order, not the total energy of a practical machine. A realistic model must identify registers, correlations, retained histories, and reset operations.

</details>
